# Code Conventions

## Application handlers

```
application/
├── commands/{use-case}/{use-case}.handler.ts   ← @CommandHandler
├── queries/{use-case}/{use-case}.handler.ts    ← @QueryHandler
└── handlers/
    ├── events/on-{event}/on-{event}.handler.ts ← @EventsHandler (subfolder per event)
    ├── workflow/{task}.handler.ts              ← @WorkflowTaskHandler
    └── queue/{job}.handler.ts                  ← @QueueHandler (+ {job}.job.ts)
```

- Register all handlers in the owning `*.module.ts` `providers` — no auto-discovery.
- Host cross-module glue: `apps/api/src/shared/integrations/{domain}/handlers/...`
- Shared packages: BullMQ processors in `infrastructure/queue/`; job classes in `application/jobs/`.

## Barrel exports

- **One** `index.ts` per module root — no nested barrels in subdirectories.
- Intra-module imports use **direct file paths**, never directory barrels.
- Module `index.ts`: explicit named exports only (no `export *`); export only the public consumer API.

## Pagination & sorting

- List endpoints: `@Query() query: PaginatedQueryDto` — never raw `pageIndex`/`pageSize` params.
- Pass into domain: `new BaseFilter(props?, pageIndex?, pageSize?, sortBy?, sortDir?)`.
- Extra filters: **extend** `PaginatedQueryDto`; constrain `sortBy` with `@IsIn([...])`.
- `SortOrder` / `BaseFilter` = domain (`@lib/core`); `PaginatedQueryDto` = presentation.
- Do **not** migrate the queue module — it uses BullMQ ranges, not `BaseFilter`.
